WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.536
-My first guests are one of the
biggest groups on the planet.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.738
They've had four number one
albums faster than any group

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.573
since The Beatles.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.609
Their latest single "Dynamite"
hit number one

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.344
on the Billboard Hot 100 chart

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:14.781
and topped the iTunes charts
in over 100 countries.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:17.250
Here is BTS!

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.052
-Here we are!
-BTS!

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:23.055
-Welcome back.
Welcome back.

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:26.893
Welcome. And thank you for being
on the show all week.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.260
I love you guys.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.831
You know, it has been two years
almost to the day

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.167
since you first came
on this show.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.569
And during that time --
-Time fast!

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.838
-I know, so fast.
During that appearance,

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.408
I asked -- I remember talking
to you guys and I said,

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:44.411
"What's next for BTS?
What's next?"

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:47.146
And Suga, do you remember
what you said?

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:49.048
-Go Grammy.
-Go Grammy!

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:50.683
-That's right, Grammys.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.451
You were like, Grammys,
Grammys, Grammys.

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:56.022
And since then, you've
presented, you've performed,

00:00:56.022 --> 00:01:00.059
and I have a feeling this year
you're going to be nominated.

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:02.661
What would a Grammy nomination
mean to you?

00:01:02.661 --> 00:01:06.131
-Yeah, the Grammys is definitely
the most honorable

00:01:06.131 --> 00:01:08.901
music award, you know,
that evaluates the prominence

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.736
and the musical odyssey
of an artist.

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:13.005
So we all grew up watching
the Grammy Awards

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.975
and we especially remember
the 2009 one

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:20.513
with the suits, T.I.,
Jay-Z, M.I.A.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.348
We just watched all of it.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:26.052
And, you know, so doing
a BTS solo performance

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.820
with our own song and
winning the Grammys

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:31.190
are kind of like awesome, and
also a dream that has naturally

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.825
grown inside us.
-Yeah.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.894
-So winning a Grammy
in such difficult times

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:38.197
could give like greater hope
and dreams to a lot of people,

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:41.433
especially our Army and Jimmy.

00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:42.969
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah!

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:45.872
That's right, well, I think
"Dynamite" couldn't have been

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.607
a bigger, bigger smash.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.375
I mean, it was massive.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.677
A lot of -- a lot of firsts
for you guys.

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:54.346
First all-English song.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:57.750
-First song to hit number one
on the Billboard Hot 100.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.984
-One!

00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:02.288
-First Korean group ever
to achieve that milestone.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.689 line:0%
-[ Speaks Korean ]

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.825 line:0%
-What was your reaction like
the night you found out

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.526
"Dynamite" was number one?
-Whoo!

00:02:07.526 --> 00:02:10.863
-We couldn't believe our eyes,
looking at the chart.

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:13.299
-Yeah.
-It felt like a dream.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.901
-Whoo!
-Whoa!

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.103
-Amazing.
-[ Shouting ]

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:19.238
-It's real?
Is this real?

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:21.073
-Ah!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:22.575
-Yo, it's real.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.310
-It's real,
it's definitely real.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.512
You had the number one song
in the world

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:27.914
for two weeks in a row.

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.448
And now it's back at number one
this week.

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:31.250
-Thanks to Jimmy!
-Yeah, Jimmy!

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.619
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:36.589
-The music video also broke
a Guinness world record

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:39.191
for the biggest music video
debut in history,

00:02:39.191 --> 00:02:43.062
over 101 million views
in its first 24 hours.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:47.166
Also the most commented on video
in YouTube history.

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:50.369
You actually weren't going to
release the song when you did.

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:52.138
Can you talk about what changed
your minds?

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:55.007
-People around the world have
been going through

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:58.577
a difficult time
because of the pandemic.

00:02:58.577 --> 00:03:02.815
We also felt discouraged
by the situation.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:07.887
So we took on a new challenge,
which was "Dynamite."

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:11.624
This project was not only
for us, but also

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:17.129
for our fans whom we wanted to
energize and give joy to

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:19.432
during this difficult period.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.767
-It couldn't have been better,
and much needed.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.869
We all needed a good song.

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:26.005
Everyone just wanted
something to listen to.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:29.208
We all -- we need content,
we need things.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:31.410
In June, you celebrated

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.580
your seven-year anniversary
as a group.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.247
How did you celebrate?
Did you party?

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:36.983 line:0%
-Oh!

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:42.055 line:0%
-Rehearsal.
-Ah, rehearsal.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:49.696 line:0%
-Sipping champagne!
-Champagne.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.365
[ Laughter ]
-Whoo!

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:55.101
-Rehearsal and champagne.

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:57.270
-That's the way to do it
right there.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.171
I know you guys miss
performing so much

00:03:59.171 --> 00:04:01.641
in front of a sold-out stadium.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:04.710
Is it hard to stay connected to
your fans during quarantine?

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.312
What do you do?

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:10.250
-We don't know when
we could meet our fans again,

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.686
but we are trying to do
whatever we can.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:17.356
We have a global
social comment card,

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:20.826
and we connect
with our army there.

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.761
-Good man, good man,
I like that.

00:04:22.761 --> 00:04:25.064
I wanted to mention,
the new movie out

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.432
called "Break the Silence."

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.101
It's in select theaters now.

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:32.104
And you just announced
the new album, "BE."

00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:33.773
-"BE"!
-"BE!"

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:36.976
-Me? Me?
-No, not me, "BE."

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.511
-"BE."
-Not "BE."

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:40.446
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:43.316
-The next album --
is the next album "T"?

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:45.284
-Yo, you got it.
-Or "P?"

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:47.219
-We're selling some new tees.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:49.121
-S!

00:04:49.121 --> 00:04:52.258
-Talk to me about "BE."
I want to know about "BE."

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:54.259
-Yo, Jimmy Fallon, let's go.

00:04:54.259 --> 00:04:55.828
[ Laughs ]
-Jimmy Fallon.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.930
-Jimmy Fallon.
-Jimmy.

00:05:22.754 --> 00:05:25.057
-Are there going to be
any more English songs?

00:05:25.057 --> 00:05:26.559
-Can you write the lyrics?

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:28.427
-No, you don't want that,
you don't want that.

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:29.829
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:31.664
-We want it!

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.666
-Stick around, I want to talk to
you about some awesome stuff

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.501
you're doing outside of music,
please.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:38.737
More with BTS when we come back.
BTS!

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:40.907
[ Cheering ]
[ Clapping ]

